I've been reading the posts about unifying Loglan and Lojban, and I have not 
 heard a single voice of dissention.
 I prefer having two distinct languages.  I admit, though, that I see very 
 little in Loglan that Lojban doesn't have, and usually done better.  
 In JCB's novel "The Troika incident" the future population uses a version of 

 the language Panlan (Loglan) about 10 versions removed from the original 
 language.  I like to think of Lojban as the second or maybe third version in 

 the series.  
 Steven Lytle

